From 5fe82055782a15b65fd410c972dc63224f71dae4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hoangvu12 <hggaming91@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 14:59:05 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] engine: the parent's host reports for children whose host
 doesn't, once their chat shows the turn

A parent's host now watches children hosted on a device without child-reports: once the child's registry row says its turn settled and its doc, synced here, shows that turn, it files the child's report under the same key a pushing host would. If the answer stays away 10 minutes on a row that answers this request, the parent hears its status alone (stage unsynced, no end anywhere), and the full end once it syncs. The still-working note says when such a child's status is unconfirmed, or when a reporting child's device is offline. A report kept from the agent under -waited or -quiet now wins over the same one held plain. Advertised as child-reports-watch.
